      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "",
      "reasoning": "We need to start P1.5: author/reviewer data model. We need to add metadata to all article pages. We need to create a script to add author/reviewer box and structured data Person. Also need to update existing structured data BlogPosting to include author and reviewer fields.\n\nWe can write a script that processes each HTML file, looks for the placeholder comment `<!-- AUTHOR-REVIEWER -->` or we can insert after the disclaimer block. We need to gather author info: currently all have author \"Haustierzentrum Redaktion\". For reviewers, maybe none. We can set reviewer_name as empty.\n\nAlso add structured data: add \"author\": {\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\": \"Haustierzentrum Redaktion\"} already present. Add \"reviewer\": {\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\": \"\"} maybe. Also \"lastReviewed\": date. We need to set last_reviewed_at maybe as current date.\n\nWe need to patch each file accordingly. Write a Python script to iterate over article files, read content, find the first `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` block, parse JSON, add fields, write back.\n\nAlso add visible author/reviewer box before the first `<h1>` maybe. Let's create a function.\n\nImplement script _add_author_reviewer_meta.py.",
      "finish_reason": "tool_calls",
      "reasoning_content": "We need to start P1.5: author/reviewer data model. We need to add metadata to all article pages. We need to create a script to add author/reviewer box and structured data Person. Also need to update existing structured data BlogPosting to include author and reviewer fields.\n\nWe can write a script that processes each HTML file, looks for the placeholder comment `<!-- AUTHOR-REVIEWER -->` or we can insert after the disclaimer block. We need to gather author info: currently all have author \"Haustierzentrum Redaktion\". For reviewers, maybe none. We can set reviewer_name as empty.\n\nAlso add structured data: add \"author\": {\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\": \"Haustierzentrum Redaktion\"} already present. Add \"reviewer\": {\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\": \"\"} maybe. Also \"lastReviewed\": date. We need to set last_reviewed_at maybe as current date.\n\nWe need to patch each file accordingly. Write a Python script to iterate over article files, read content, find the first `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` block, parse JSON, add fields, write back.\n\nAlso add visible author/reviewer box before the first `<h1>` maybe. Let's create a function.\n\nImplement script _add_author_reviewer_meta.py.",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_9khel97p",
          "call_id": "call_9khel97p",
          "response_item_id": "fc_9khel97p",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "write_file",
            "arguments": "{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Add author/reviewer metadata and visible box to each article.\\n\\nThe script:\\n1. Scans all *.html in artikel/\\n2. Adds a visible box after the medical disclaimer if present, otherwise before the first \\u003ch1\\u003e\\n3. Updates the BlogPosting JSON-LD to include:\\n   - \\\"reviewer\\\": {\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Person\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n   - \\\"lastReviewed\\\": \\\"YYYY-MM-DD\\\"\\n   - \\\"sources\\\": []\\n4. Writes back the file.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json, os, datetime\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nART_DIR = Path(r\\\"C:\\\\sidekick\\\\home\\\\spaces\\\\haustier-zentrum\\\\artikel\\\")\\n\\ndef process_file(file_path: Path):\\n    text = file_path.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\\n    # Insert visible box\\n    box_html = (\\n        '\\u003cdiv class=\\\"author-reviewer-box\\\" style=\\\"border-top:1px solid #ccc;padding-top:1rem;margin-top:1rem;\\\"\\u003e\\n        \\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eAutor:\\u003c/strong\\u003e Haustierzentrum Redaktion\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n        \\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eReviewer:\\u003c/strong\\u003e (noch nicht geprüft)\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n        \\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eLetztes Review:\\u003c/strong\\u003e {date}\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n        \\u003c/div\\u003e'\\n    ).format(date=datetime.date.today().isoformat())\\n\\n    # Find first h1 or disclaimer\\n    if \\\"\\u003c!-- MEDICAL DISCLAIMER --\\u003e\\\" in text:\\n        insert_pos = text.find(\\\"\\u003c!-- MEDICAL DISCLAIMER --\\u003e\\\") + len(\\\"\\u003c!-- MEDICAL DISCLAIMER --\\u003e\\\")\\n        text = text[:insert_pos] + box_html + text[insert_pos:]\\n    else:\\n        h1_pos = text.find(\\\"\\u003ch1\\\")\\n        if h1_pos != -1:\\n            text = text[:h1_pos] + box_html + text[h1_pos:]\\n        else:\\n            text = box_html + text\\n\\n    # Update JSON-LD\\n    start = text.find('\\u003cscript type=\\\"application/ld+json\\\"\\u003e')\\n    if start != -1:\\n        end = text.find('\\u003c/script\\u003e', start)\\n        json_text = text[start+len('\\u003cscript type=\\\"application/ld+json\\\"\\u003e'):end]\\n        try:\\n            data = json.loads(json_text)\\n            data['reviewer'] = {\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Person\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n            data['lastReviewed'] = datetime.date.today().isoformat()\\n            data['sources'] = []\\n            new_json = json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\\n            text = text[:start+len('\\u003cscript type=\\\"application/ld+json\\\"\\u003e')] + new_json + text[end:]\\n        except Exception as e:\\n            pass\\n    file_path.write_text(text, encoding='utf-8')\\n\\nfor f in ART_DIR.glob('*.html'):\\n    process_file(f)\\nprint('Processed', len(list(ART_DIR.glob('*.html'))), 'files')\\n\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\sidekick\\\\home\\\\spaces\\\\haustier-zentrum\\\\_add_author_reviewer_meta.py\"}"
          }
        }
