      "content": "**What We Have Accomplished**\n\n| # | Task | Status |\n|---|------|--------|\n| 1 | **Sitemap** – `sitemap.xml` now returns 200, is a valid sitemap‑index that includes `sitemap-articles.xml`, `sitemap-categories.xml` and `sitemap-static.xml`. The sections only contain 200‑canonical URLs. |\n| 2 | **Legal Pages** – `/impressum/` now only shows the Impressum, `/datenschutz/` is a separate page. Footer link points to `/datenschutz/`. Cookie‑banner “Mehr Infos” links to `/datenschutz.html`. |\n| 3 | **Consent‑Management** – Added the consent scripts to all article pages. Atomically removed any possible third‑party loads before the user gives consent (AdSense, Amazon tracking, analytics, fonts). All consent options (Akzeptieren, Ablehnen, Einstellungen) are functional and stored. |\n| 4 | **Health Content Governance** – Every health article gets a visible disclaimer, author box, reviewer box (placeholder) and a “Letztes Review” date. The JSON‑LD section now contains the required `reviewer`, `lastReviewed`, and an empty `sources` array. All missing articles are processed. |\n| 5 | **Affiliate Governance** – Created `/affiliate-hinweis.html`. All product boxes that previously existed inline in health articles are now wrapped in a label “Affiliate‑Link” with a link to the hint page. Health‑specific boxes are separated from medical content by a blank line. |\n| 6 | **Trust‑Claims** – Scanned the entire site for strong trust claims (e.g., “100 % artgerecht”) and flagged them. The `redaktionelle-standards/` page has been drafted to provide evidence, sources, and explanation for each claim. |\n| 7 | **Red‑Flag Checker** – A script was planned to flag sensitive medical claims without sources (dosierung, vergiftung, etc.). The script is still in development but the scaffolding and a list of triggers is ready. |\n| 8 | **Structured Data** – All articles now contain a `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` block with `BlogPosting` type that includes `author`, `reviewer`, `lastReviewed`, and `sources`. |\n| 9 | **Canonical & Routing** – All URLs have been canonicalized to use extension‑less, trailing‑slash URLs. 301 redirects are in place where needed. |\n|10 | **Semantic Tables** – Reviewed tables and determined that some need to be converted to real `<table>` elements with `<caption>`, `<th>` and `<tbody>`. Work is still in progress for a subset. |\n|11 | **Internal Linking & Hubs** – Core hubs such as `/hunde/gesundheit/` and `/katzen/ernährung/` exist. Articles will get 3–6 relevant internal links. Orphaned articles have been identified. Next step will be to implement these links. |\n\n**Next Steps for Upcoming Session**\n\n1. Finalize the **Safety Red‑Flag Checker** and run it across all health articles.  \n2. Apply **semantic‑table rendering** for all remaining tables.  \n3. Complete **internal linking hub strategy** and refine the anchor texts.  \n4. Add real reviewer names, credentials, and actual sources where we can find them.  \n5. Perform a full LSCP + SEO audit to ensure no 404/500/redirect loops remain.\n\nPlease let me know which of these tasks you'd like to tackle next.",
