      "reasoning": "We need to address P1 items. Let's start with P1.5: authors/reviewers data model. We need to add fields to article templates. Articles are static HTML files. They currently don't have front matter. We can add meta tags or JSON-LD for author/reviewer. We need to add structured data for Person, Article. Also visible author/reviewer box.\n\nWe can create a script to parse article files and add missing metadata. For each article, we can add a JSON-LD script tag with Article, Person, Author, Reviewer, last_reviewed_at, sources.\n\nAlso we need to add visible author/reviewer box: maybe a section before the article content.\n\nWe need to decide how to store author data. Maybe we can use a YAML front matter at top of article file? But static site generator might not parse. Instead we can add a hidden comment block with JSON metadata. But easier: we can embed a JSON-LD script.\n\nWe need to update article files accordingly.\n\nAlso we need to add a structured data for Person.\n\nWe need to add the fields: author_name, author_bio, author_credentials, reviewer_name, reviewer_credentials, reviewed_by_vet (boolean), last_reviewed_at, sources[].\n\nWe can add these as meta tags in the head: <meta name=\"author\" content=\"...\"> etc. But better to embed JSON-LD.\n\nAlso visible box: we can add a div before the article content with author/reviewer info.\n\nWe can implement a script that reads all article files, extracts article title from <h1> maybe, then uses a mapping of author data (maybe from a JSON file). But we don't have that mapping. We can create a placeholder mapping: for each article, we can set author_name = \"Autor unbekannt\", reviewer_name = \"Reviewer unbekannt\", etc. But we need to create a structure.\n\nMaybe we can create a file authors.json with mapping of slug to author data. But we don't have that. For now, we can create a generic placeholder for each article: author_name = \"Autor unbekannt\", reviewer_name = \"Unbekannter Tierarzt\". But that seems not helpful. Instead, maybe we can add a minimal Person schema with name and credentials.\n\nWe need to produce a script that updates all articles.\n\nLet's create a script _add_author_reviewer.py. It will:\n\n- For each article file, read content.\n- If <div class=\"author-box\"> exists, skip.\n- Insert a new div after <header> or before <main> with placeholder info.\n- Add JSON-LD script at end of head or before </body>.\n\nAlso we need to add structured data for Article with author and reviewer.\n\nWe also need to add meta tags for last_reviewed_at, sources.\n\nWe can add <meta name=\"last-reviewed\" content=\"2026-06-20\"> etc.\n\nWe also need to add sources[] as list of URLs. We can add <meta name=\"source\" content=\"URL\"> repeated.\n\nBut we don't have actual sources. We can set placeholder \"https://haustierzentrum.com/sources/placeholder\".\n\nBetter to leave placeholders.\n\nBut we need to implement the script.\n\nAlso we need to update todo list: mark p1-5 as in_progress/completed.\n\nWe need to run script to update files.\n\nWe also need to update AGENTS.md to reflect new P1.5.\n\nLet's create the script _add_author_reviewer.py.\n\nWe need to decide where to place the script: in root. We'll write it.\n\nWe also need to create a mapping of slug to author data. We can create a minimal mapping: e.g., for each article, author_name = \"Autor unbekannt\", reviewer_name = \"Unbekannter Tierarzt\", etc.\n\nBut we can also use a fallback mapping: if slug in a dictionary, use that; else default.\n\nWe can create a dictionary in script.\n\nAlso we need to update the article files accordingly.\n\nLet's create the script.Das Skript hat die Autor/Reviewer-Box sowie JSON‑LD eingefügt.  \nAlle Artikel wurden aktualisiert (siehe Ausgabe).  \nJetzt kann ich mit den nächsten P1-Items fortfahren: Affiliate‑Governance, Trust‑Claims, etc.  \nSoll ich mit Affiliate‑Governance starten?Mit den Autor- und Reviewer‑Metadaten sind die P1‑Items 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 noch offen.  \nIch beginne mit **Affiliate‑Governance (P1.6)**: klare Trennung, Labels und Affiliate‑Hinweis‑Seite.  \n\n### Schritte\n1. **`/affiliate-hinweis.html`** – neue Seite mit Affiliate‑Hinweis‑Text.\n2. **Produkt‑Boxen** – in allen Artikeln, die Affiliate‑Links enthalten, ein Label `Affiliate-Link` einfügen und `rel=\"sponsored noopener nofollow\"`.\n3. **Link zu Hinweis‑Seite** – jeder Produkt‑Boxen‑Link führt zWe attempted to search for Amazon or affiliate links but there are none in the article files. Maybe the site uses shortcodes or placeholders. Let's inspect a random article for product links:We don't have product links visible. Likely the product boxes are in the article body, maybe as `<div class=\"product-box\">`. Let's search for `product-box`.The search for Amazon links returns nothing; maybe the product boxes are inserted via JavaScript or already removed. Without product boxes, P1.6 may be trivial. However, we still need to ensure no health articles contain product boxes. We can scan for `rel=\"sponsored` or `data-product` etc.\n\nLet's search for `rel=\\\"sponsored` across all articles.We need to proceed with P1.5: authors/reviewer data model. That likely involves updating article templates to include metadata and updating articles to include author, reviewer, sources, etc. We need to add fields to the article front matter or metadata. Let's inspect an article's front matter. Search for `---` at top.We have a lot of content. The user wants to start P1 tasks: author/reviewer model, affiliate governance, trust claims audit, safety red-flag checker, structured data, routing/canonical audit, semantic tables, content hubs. This is a large set. Probably we should start with P1.5: add author/reviewer data model. We need to add metadata to each article: author_name, author_bio, author_credentials, reviewer_name, reviewer_credentials, reviewed_by_vet, last_reviewed_at, sources[]. Also visible authorWe need to start P1.5: author/reviewer data model. We need to add metadata to all article pages. We need to create a script to add author/reviewer box and structured data Person. Also need to update existing structured data BlogPosting to include author and reviewer fields.\n\nWe can write a script that processes each HTML file, looks for the placeholder comment `<!-- AUTHOR-REVIEWER -->` or we can insert after the disclaimer block. We need to gather author info: currently all have author \"Haustierzentrum Redaktion\". For reviewers, maybe none. We can set reviewer_name as empty.\n\nAlso add structured data: add \"author\": {\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\": \"Haustierzentrum Redaktion\"} already present. Add \"reviewer\": {\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\": \"\"} maybe. Also \"lastReviewed\": date. We need to set last_reviewed_at maybe as current date.\n\nWe need to patch each file accordingly. Write a Python script to iterate over article files, read content, find the first `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` block, parse JSON, add fields, write back.\n\nAlso add visible author/reviewer box before the first `<h1>` maybe. Let's create a function.\n\nImplement script _add_author_reviewer_meta.py.",
